                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1139: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Agent
                        and Consul General at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Blake</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-05T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                                1925—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9. In order to remove any misapprehensions which may have been caused by the
                    reported enlistments of American citizens in the Sultan’s Army, it is suggested
                    that you may consider the advisability of taking measures to invite the
                    attention of American citizens in Morocco to the provisions of Sections 5282 and
                    4090, Revised Statutes of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
